ptance\":[{\"criterion\":\"A filter setting on a device or group changes the filtering of that device only\",\"met\":true,\"evidence\":\"In testDeviceAndGroupSettings, device 1 (no attributes) is still filtered by the server config. Device 2 sets filter.invalid=false and filter.future=0, and its invalid and future positions pass. The group of devices 3 and 4 sets filter.static=true, so device 3 drops static positions. Device 4 sets filter.static=false on itself, which overrides the group.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The change is covered by tests\",\"met\":true,\"evidence\":\"Added FilterHandlerTest.testDeviceAndGroupSettings and testDefaultFuture; both pass.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The existing test suite still passes\",\"met\":true,\"evidence\":\"./gradlew test checkstyleMain checkstyleTest with JAVA_HOME=openjdk@25: 614 tests, 0 failures/errors, checkstyle clean.\"}],\"human_needed\":[],\"harness_used\":[\"Existing FilterHandlerTest and the Mockito/JUnit setup\",\"AttributeUtil.lookup, the existing per-device lookup (already used by filter.calendar and filter.skipAttributes)\",\"Gradle test and checkstyle tasks\"],\"harness_gaps\":[{\"file\":null,\"problem\":\"The repository has no agent instructions (CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md) and no note on the required JDK. The default JDK 17 fails with 'invalid source release: 21'; I had to find openjdk@25 myself.\"},{\"file\":\"src/test/java/org/traccar/handler/FilterHandlerTest.java\",\"problem\":\"The old test stubbed typed Config getters (getBoolean/getLong). AttributeUtil.lookup reads config.getString, so after the change those stubs had no effect and every test had to be moved to getString stubs.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"done","summary":"The 15 filter settings you listed are now device keys (KeyType.CONFIG plus KeyType.DEVICE), so they can be set on a device or a group. FilterHandler now resolves each setting for the position's device with AttributeUtil.lookup: the device attribute first, then its groups, then the server configuration, then the key default. With nothing configured, filter.future still filters positions more than 86400 s in the future. A value of 0 or false still disables a filter. The constructor is now FilterHandler(CacheManager, StatisticsManager), and MainModule was updated to match. filter.globalDailyLimit was not in your list, so it is still server-only: it is read from cacheManager.getConfig() for each position. The full test suite passes (614 tests, 0 failures) and checkstyleMain/checkstyleTest pass, run with JDK 25 because the project needs Java 21 or newer.","changes":[{"path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/config/Keys.java","summary":"Added KeyType.DEVICE to filter.invalid, zero, duplicate, outdated, future, past, accuracy, approximate, static, distance, maxSpeed, minPeriod, dailyLimit, dailyLimitInterval and skipLimit."},{"path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/handler/FilterHandler.java","summary":"Removed the Config constructor parameter and the cached fields. Each filter now resolves its setting for the position's device through AttributeUtil.lookup; a missing value with no default means disabled (false or 0). The global daily limit is read from the server configuration for each position."},{"path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/MainModule.java","summary":"provideFilterHandler now calls new FilterHandler(cacheManager, statisticsManager)."},{"path":"src/test/java/org/traccar/handler/FilterHandlerTest.java","summary":"Updated to the new constructor; the config mock now stubs getString, which is what lookup reads. The passing handler now sets filter.future=0, because the default now applies. Added testDefaultFuture (the 86400 s default) and testDeviceAndGroupSettings: the server config applies to a device without attributes; device attributes disable invalid and future filtering for that device only; a group attribute enables static filtering for its devices; a device attribute takes priority over its group."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"A filter setting on a device or